        <span class="k">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"Else block is executing"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">func</span><span class="p">()</span> 
<span class="c1"># Else block will be executed
# a is not bigger than 1
# Else block is executing</span></code></pre></figure>

<p>In this example, a is declared as an integer and its value is 1. After the if-else blocks, we call <code class="highlighter-rouge">func()</code> and program executes <strong>else</strong> block, because <em>“a is not bigger than 1”</em>. So, in this case, function declarations was executed and produced output. If we were declared a with bigger than 1, i.e. 9, the program would be executed <strong>if</strong> block and prints out the <code class="highlighter-rouge">a is bigger than 1</code> <code class="highlighter-rouge">If block is executing</code> messages.</p>

